    <string name="about">About</string>
    <string name="about_text">Temper is free and open source. No ads, no account, no internet access. Part of Stillcraft, small tools for a quieter mind.</string>
    <string name="disclaimer">Temper is not medical advice. Cold water and heat strain the heart and circulation; ask a doctor first if you have any condition, and never go into open water alone.</string>
    <string name="about_version">Version %s</string>

    <!-- Onboarding -->
    <string name="ob_title">Temper</string>
    <string name="ob_text">A smith tempers steel with fire and water. You can temper yourself the same way: cold water, contrast showers, the sauna.</string>
    <string name="ob_text2">Every session folds a new layer into your own Damascus blade. Practise and it glows; leave it and it cools.</string>
    <string name="ob_ways">Three ways to temper</string>
    <string name="ob_cold">A shower, a bath, a lake or an ice hole. Calm breathing first, a target time, a guide through the first 30 seconds and warming up after.</string>
    <string name="ob_contrast">Hot and cold by a voice from behind the curtain. Ready programs or your own.</string>
    <string name="ob_sauna">The phone stays outside: it tells you when to come out by the clock, then leads the plunge and the rest.</string>
